From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 18:04:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01833/11362] [outer-loop] detector: diffusion-first
 restructure + GPU AR finalizer (CUDA llama.cpp)

Operator asked for GPU acceleration over an overnight CPU run. Findings:
- vLLM blocked on gemma-4 (per-layer num_key_value_heads list crashes its transformers).
- llama-perplexity is corpus-only (needs >=2x ctx tokens); won't score single steps.
- Built llama-cpp-python from source with -DGGML_CUDA=on (arch 86) in an isolated 3.12
  venv; VERIFIED GPU offload (all layers -> CUDA0 RTX 3090, 9s load).
Detector split into: phase-1 diffusion-surprisal (headline, llama.cpp PR binary, CPU but
fast ~6s/item) writing an interim AUROC; phase-2 AR-perplexity now on GPU via the CUDA wheel
(exp_ar_perplexity_gpu_finalize.py). max_tokens=1 (NOT 0=unlimited) + exact step-token slice.
Matched baseline: same gemma-4-26B-A4B backbone + Q4_K_M quant; both verifier_is_oracle=false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
